   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} \\) and \\( dv = x \\, dx \\), so \\( du = \\frac{1}{x} \\, dx \\) and \\( v = \\frac{x^{2}}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Power",
               "x",
               2
            ],
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then the integral equals \\( \\left[\\frac{x^{2} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}}{2}\\right]_{1}^{2} - \\int_{1}^{2} \\frac{x}{2} \\, dx \\), and the boundary term is \\( 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            [
               "Ln",
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The remaining integral is \\( \\int_{1}^{2} \\frac{x}{2} \\, dx = \\frac{3}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            3,
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So the value is \\( 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} - \\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right) = - \\frac{3}{4} + 2 \\ln{\\left(2 \\right)} \\).",
